---
description: PHP architecture and structure rules
globs: ["**/*.php"]
---

PHP Architecture Rules:

- Follow PSR-4 namespace structure
- Follow PSR-12 formatting

- Use the existing autoloader:
  ./src/Autoloader.php

- Namespace root is:
  Trefik\

- Place all classes inside:
  ./includes

- Namespace and file path must match exactly

Examples:
- Trefik\Core\Plugin -> includes/Core/Plugin.php
- Trefik\Ajax\CartAjaxHandler -> includes/Ajax/CartAjaxHandler.php
- Trefik\Integrations\Wixmo\Api\StudentApi -> includes/Integrations/Wixmo/Api/StudentApi.php

- Do NOT use manual require/include for classes

- Keep classes:
  - Small
  - Focused
  - Single responsibility

- Reuse existing classes/helpers before creating new ones

- Prefer existing architecture in:
  - Core
  - Ajax
  - Admin
  - Frontend
  - Shortcodes
  - Integrations

- Avoid:
  - Large rewrites
  - Duplicate logic
  - Unnecessary abstractions
  - New utility layers without clear need
  - Random helper classes when existing helpers/config/base classes already exist

- Maintain naming consistency:
  - Classes
  - Methods
  - Namespaces
  - Integration folders

- Keep logic separated:
  - Business logic
  - API logic
  - UI / presentation logic
  - AJAX request handling
  - Hook registration / bootstrap responsibilities

- Prefer composition over inheritance where practical

- Before expanding existing code, first verify whether the class is actively used through:
  - bootstrap logic
  - instantiation
  - hook registration
  - register_hooks() calls

- Do NOT assume that existing classes are active just because they exist in the repository

- Treat commented-out or legacy code as inactive unless explicitly instructed otherwise

- Write predictable, maintainable, production-minded code